From b37cb77a1b5c788d74cd8aff405c446f1956ce10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:23:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] OpenVPN Killswitch only for a full-tunnel client; VPN pages
 name the real state

- Policy Routing closed a device's traffic for a client with a stored Killswitch even when the
  client was set to Redirect Internet traffic: No, or was a TAP client - cases where the
  Killswitch row is hidden and nothing is meant to be forced into the tunnel. The fail-closed rule
  now needs Redirect = All or VPN Director, and a TUN client.
- VPN Director shows the effective Killswitch. The client page asks before a stored Killswitch
  comes back into force when Redirect leaves No, and restarts routing when the interface type
  changes.
- VPN Director and Policy Routing name the state of a target: client off, not in VPN Director
  mode, pushed routes only, TAP. The warnings for a switched-off client no longer say its
  Killswitch blocks traffic: that traffic uses the WAN, except on a guest network bound to the
  client with its own Kill Switch on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
